+After carefully reviewing the provided code changes and test cases across all files, I found no blocking correctness issues. The implementation follows solid patterns for manifest validation, measurement, and testing.The Zod schema in `manifest.ts` correctly enforces constraints on mod IDs, semver ranges, and contribution IDs. The validation logic thoroughly checks for:- Executable vs. declarative execution modes- Duplicate IDs and paths- Valid semver ranges- Proper inclusion of `agon.mod.json` in pack files- Correct contribution types for each execution modeThe measurement script (`measure-modular-slice1a.mjs`) properly:- Sets up isolated environments for testing- Handles cold start measurements with error checking- Validates RSS values with regex patterns- Calculates percentiles correctly- Ensures proper file path handlingAll test cases in `modular-manifest.test.ts` cover critical edge cases:- ID length constraints- Invalid path patterns- Declarative mode restrictions- Semver range validation- Contribution ID patterns- Asset path validationThe code handles null/undefined values appropriately and follows strict validation patterns. There are no off-by-one errors or boundary cases that would cause incorrect behavior in the current implementation.The most important aspect is that the manifest validation ensures immutability through `deepFreeze` while maintaining all required constraints. The measurement script properly handles the edge cases that could cause false positives in performance testing.I found no blocking issues that would prevent the code from working correctly. The implementation is robust and covers all critical edge cases through both code validation and test cases.<!--AGON_REVIEW_FINDINGS_v1-->```json[]```
